Trimmed real data (ruling T1: GitHub download counts are open data).

assets.jsonl holds 18 release assets of 6 repositories (JetBrains/JetBrainsMono,
IBM/plex, subframe7536/maple-font, microsoft/cascadia-code, be5invis/Iosevka,
githubnext/monaspace), copied from the github_releases snapshot of 2026-09-26
in the extract format of assets.jsonl.gz: repository, release tag, publish
time, prerelease flag, asset name, asset creation time and download count.
Nothing else is kept: no author, uploader, release notes or URLs, so no
personal data. The tests add a few synthetic rows (repositories under
example-org, googlefonts/Inconsolata's asset, and asset names no release
carries), marked as such in test_github_repos.py.

Source: https://docs.github.com/en/rest/releases/releases and
https://docs.github.com/en/graphql (the repositories' public releases).
GitHub's Acceptable Use Policies allow collecting public, non-personal
information through the API.
